From: PTPT52.AI <ptpt52@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 10:15:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: use 1K AN7563 hardware-forwarding payloads

The EN7523-family vendor firmware boots with qdma_init=0x11.  Both QDMA
instances consequently use 16384 hardware-forwarding descriptors with
1024-byte payloads.  The vendor kernel reserves one 16 MiB payload region
for each QDMA with 64 KiB alignment.

The common driver already derives the hardware-forwarding descriptor count
from each reserved-memory region, but selects a 2 KiB payload for QDMA0.
Use 1 KiB payloads on both AN7563 QDMA instances so each 16 MiB region maps
to the vendor's 16384 descriptors.  Keep the existing payload selection on
other SoCs.

Signed-off-by: PTPT52.AI <ptpt52@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c | 9 ++++++---
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -1529,6 +1529,7 @@ static int airoha_qdma_init_hfwd_queues(
 	int size, index, num_desc = HW_DSCP_NUM;
 	struct airoha_eth *eth = qdma->eth;
 	int id = qdma - &eth->qdma[0];
+	bool payload_1k = eth->soc->version == 0x7563 || id;
 	u32 status, buf_size;
 	dma_addr_t dma_addr;
 	const char *name;
@@ -1537,7 +1538,8 @@ static int airoha_qdma_init_hfwd_queues(
 	if (!name)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
-	buf_size = id ? AIROHA_MAX_PACKET_SIZE / 2 : AIROHA_MAX_PACKET_SIZE;
+	buf_size = payload_1k ? AIROHA_MAX_PACKET_SIZE / 2 :
+				AIROHA_MAX_PACKET_SIZE;
 	index = of_property_match_string(eth->dev->of_node,
 					 "memory-region-names", name);
 	if (index >= 0) {
@@ -1576,10 +1578,11 @@ static int airoha_qdma_init_hfwd_queues(
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
 	airoha_qdma_wr(qdma, REG_FWD_DSCP_BASE, dma_addr);
-	/* QDMA0: 2KB. QDMA1: 1KB */
+	/* AN7563 uses 1KB on both QDMAs; other SoCs use 2KB on QDMA0. */
 	airoha_qdma_rmw(qdma, REG_HW_FWD_DSCP_CFG,
 			HW_FWD_DSCP_PAYLOAD_SIZE_MASK,
-			FIELD_PREP(HW_FWD_DSCP_PAYLOAD_SIZE_MASK, !!id));
+			FIELD_PREP(HW_FWD_DSCP_PAYLOAD_SIZE_MASK,
+				   payload_1k));
 	airoha_qdma_rmw(qdma, REG_FWD_DSCP_LOW_THR, FWD_DSCP_LOW_THR_MASK,
 			FIELD_PREP(FWD_DSCP_LOW_THR_MASK, 128));
 	airoha_qdma_rmw(qdma, REG_LMGR_INIT_CFG,
